# Corpses of the Lost: "Skeletons you control get +1/+0 and have haste" is about any Skeleton, token or card, and only
# the ones Bot1 controls. Turn 1 Bot1 casts Corpses of the Lost (Swamp, Mox Jet, Mox Ruby) and Emperor of Bones (Mox Pearl,
# Mox Emerald): its Emperor is a 3/2 with haste and attacks at once. On turn 2 Bot2 casts its own Emperor of Bones (Mox Jet, Mox
# Ruby): a Skeleton Bot1 does not control, so it stays a 2/2 and is summoning sick (no haste).

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Mox Emerald
Corpses of the Lost
Emperor of Bones
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Emperor of Bones
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Corpses of the Lost.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Emperor of Bones.Cast
Bot1.Attack(Emperor of Bones > Bot2)
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Emperor of Bones.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main2]
? Bot2.Battlefield.Emperor of Bones.SummoningSick = true
? Bot1.Battlefield.Emperor of Bones.SummoningSick = false

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 17
Bot1.Battlefield.Emperor of Bones.Power = 3
Bot1.Battlefield.Emperor of Bones.Keywords = Haste
Bot2.Battlefield.Emperor of Bones.Power = 2
Bot2.Battlefield.Emperor of Bones.Keywords = (absent)
